    "updated_at": "2016-03-24T17:42:13Z",
    "body": "Wouldn't that extend to _all_ uses of width/height (besides the \"both 0\" case)?  It sounds like the \"allowed\" usages of width/height are just to manually adjust the resolution of the image, which is better done with srcset now, right?\n\nAlso, it would be good to also specify what you just said - that they shouldnt' be used _because CSS should be used instead_.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
