    "created_at": "2016-03-24T19:38:28Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-24T19:38:28Z",
    "body": "@zcorpan The idea is that the authoring requirements allowing use of width/height to adjust the apparent density of the image probably existed solely to fill a functionality hole, which has since been plugged.  It's now _much_ better to write `<img srcset=\"200x100@2x.jpg 2x\">` than `<img width=200 height=100 src=\"400x200.jpg\">`.  Authoring conformance is all about guiding people to the right tools, after all.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
