    "created_at": "2016-03-27T22:13:11Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-27T22:13:11Z",
    "body": "I'm fine with width/height used at all times. ^_^\n\nBut you can actually allow width/height without pretending that using w/h is the right way to adjust the resolution by just removing all the \"target ratio\" stuff entirely.  Say that width/height must match the intrinsic width/height of the resource, which is already half-there (the intrinsic dimensions are adjusted by the resolution automatically).\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
